From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:07:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: ship the CHRE daemon again, disabled

0027 stopped packaging chre_daemon_msm because it could not reach the
SLPI and exited badly enough, often enough, to trip init's
updatable-crash path and reboot the device.

It is back so the failure can be retested without a rebuild each time,
but it cannot run on its own: system/chre 0001 marks the service
'disabled' so init never starts it, and 'oneshot' so init never restarts
it if it is started by hand. Neither path can reach that counter now.

The retest it was brought back for has already answered. With the SLPI
sensor registry relabeled and adsprpcd denials at zero, the daemon gets
further than before -- fastrpc opens, the user PD is created -- and then
fails exactly as it did:

  remote_handle_open_domain: dynamic loading failed for chre_slpi on
  domain 0 (dlerror undefined symbol #25 __sensors_island_start)

That symbol comes from the SLPI sensors image, so the failure is inside
DSP blobs paired with firmware from the same factory image, and there is
nothing left to fix from the Android side. CHRE does not work on this
device. Costs Active Edge; the other nanoapps it would host (activity,
geofence, smartbatching, ambient) have no consumer on a build without
GApps.

Kept rather than dropped because it is inert and makes the next retest,
after some future blob update, one command instead of a build.
---
 device-lineage.mk | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device-lineage.mk b/device-lineage.mk
index 8888cd1d..523735ce 100644
--- a/device-lineage.mk
+++ b/device-lineage.mk
@@ -70,8 +70,14 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
 # exit before sys.boot_completed and sets sys.init.updatable_crashing, which makes apexd revert
 # and reboot. 0021 already dropped the context hub HAL, so nothing consumes CHRE anyway -- do not
 # ship the daemon until the DSP side works.
-#PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
-#    chre_daemon_msm
+#
+# 2026-09-22: shipped again to retest. The SLPI sensor registry under
+# /mnt/vendor/persist/sensors was unlabeled, and adsprpcd was denied reading it 127 times a boot;
+# that is fixed now, so the DSP side may come up differently. The service is disabled in its own
+# rc so nothing starts it at boot -- start it by hand and read the log. Until that is answered it
+# must not be able to reach init's updatable-crash path again.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    chre_daemon_msm
 
 # Display
 $(call soong_config_set,qtidisplay,drmpp,true)
